Created a bucket using the Google Cloud Console.

gcloud storage buckets list

Bucket:

gs://qwiklabs-gcp-04-2ca80f6baee4-console
Task 2 — Access Cloud Shell

Cloud Shell provides:

Command-line access to a temporary Compute Engine VM
5 GB persistent storage in /home
Pre-installed Google Cloud SDK tools
Built-in authorization for Google Cloud resources
Task 3 — Create a bucket using Cloud Shell
gcloud storage buckets create gs://qwiklabs-gcp-04-2ca80f6baee4-bucket2

Verify the buckets:

gcloud storage buckets list
Task 4 — Upload a file to a Storage bucket

Create a test file:

echo "Cloud Shell Lab Task 4" > my_file.txt

Verify the file:

ls -l my_file.txt

Upload it to Cloud Storage:

gcloud storage cp my_file.txt gs://qwiklabs-gcp-04-2ca80f6baee4-bucket2/

Verify the uploaded file:

gcloud storage ls gs://qwiklabs-gcp-04-2ca80f6baee4-bucket2/
Task 5 — Create a persistent state in Cloud Shell

Set the region:

INFRACLASS_REGION=us-east4

Verify:

echo $INFRACLASS_REGION

Create the configuration directory:

mkdir infraclass

Create the configuration file:

touch infraclass/config

Save the region:

echo INFRACLASS_REGION=$INFRACLASS_REGION >> ~/infraclass/config

Set the project ID:

INFRACLASS_PROJECT_ID=qwiklabs-gcp-04-2ca80f6baee4

Save the project ID:

echo INFRACLASS_PROJECT_ID=$INFRACLASS_PROJECT_ID >> ~/infraclass/config

Load the variables:

source infraclass/config

Verify:

echo $INFRACLASS_PROJECT_ID

Configure .profile:

nano .profile

Add:

source infraclass/config

After reopening Cloud Shell, verify persistence:

echo $INFRACLASS_PROJECT_ID
